        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/id": "0bcc9f93-4f3c-5124-8641-edf082f5099b",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x) = 6\\log_{5} x\\ln x$, find $f^{\u2032}(x)$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=6\\log_{5} x$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =(6\\log_{5} x)^{\u2032}\\ln x+6\\log_{5} x(\\ln x)^{\u2032} \\\\  & =(\\frac{6}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}})(\\ln x)+(6\\log_{5} x)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\log_{5} x}{x} + \\frac{6\\ln x}{x\\ln 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
