        ":question/id": "18f3eb93-e574-5f5a-8279-040ddcf04567",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x) = x^{-2}\\log_{4} x$, find $f^{\u2032}(x)$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x^{-2}$ and $v(x)=\\log_{4} x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =(x^{-2})^{\u2032}\\log_{4} x+x^{-2}(\\log_{4} x)^{\u2032} \\\\  & =(- \\frac{2}{x^{3}})(\\log_{4} x)+(x^{-2})(\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}) \\\\  & =x^{-3}(-2\\log_{4} x + \\frac{1}{\\ln 4})\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
